;; Two separate problems with datalevin.core's with-transaction, needing two
;; separate entries:
;;
;; 1. It is published by `(datalevin.util/import-macro conn/with-transaction)`
;;    rather than a `def`, so static analysis sees no var and reports every use
;;    as unresolved. import-macro is potemkin's, near enough that clj-kondo's
;;    built-in import-vars handling picks the imported vars up — all four of
;;    datalevin.core's (with-transaction, with-transaction-kv, with-conn,
;;    with-kv). Preferred over excluding datalevin.core from :unresolved-var,
;;    which would also silence real typos like `d/no-such-fn`.
;;    Needs the dependency cache: clj-kondo --lint "$(clojure -Spath)"
;;    --dependencies --parallel --copy-configs
;;
;; 2. Knowing the var exists is not knowing it binds. Its binding vector is
;;    `[tx conn]`, which with-open already models, so without this the bound
;;    symbol reads as unresolved. (with-transaction also takes a third opts
;;    element; lint-as would call that an odd binding count, but nothing here
;;    uses that arity.)
;; 3. Our own with-tx macros bind a symbol the same way, and are the supported
;;    way to write inside a transaction — without these, every use reports the
;;    bound symbol as unresolved.
{:lint-as {datalevin.util/import-macro     potemkin/import-vars
           datalevin.core/with-transaction clojure.core/with-open
           dtlv-audit.journal/with-tx      clojure.core/with-open
           dtlv-audit.core/with-tx         clojure.core/with-open}}
